versial example. Let\u2019s say we have a ONE side model, God. The MANY side model would be Human. Each God could have MANY Humans following him/her through a JOIN model of GuardianAngel. The God model could have many GuardianAngels but lets say s/he doesn\u2019t care about keeping track of all his/her follower Humans. Who said DB associations were boring?","topics":[],"score":184450,"global_rank":393265},{"name":"MargeRosen/horoscope","owner":"MargeRosen","html_url":"https://github.com/MargeRosen/horoscope","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":184450,"global_rank":393267},{"name":"MargeRosen/webdev_quest","owner":"MargeRosen","html_url":"https://github.com/MargeRosen/webdev_quest","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":184450,"global_rank":393268},{"name":"nglasgow/Travel_Insight","owner":"nglasgow","html_url":"https://github.com/nglasgow/Travel_Insight","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":184450,"global_rank":393270},{"name":"bvuongx/Recipes_you_name_it","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/Recipes_you_name_it","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":184450,"global_rank":393273},{"name":"bvuongx/Recipes","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/Recipes","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":184450,"global_rank":393274},{"name":"ColetteIsabella/question_app","owner":"ColetteIsabella","html_url":"https://github.com/ColetteIsabella/question_app","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":184442,"global_rank":393290},{"name":"bvuongx/membership","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/membership","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language"